## DEFINITION
MEGA X (Molecular Evolutionary Genetics Analysis X) is a software package used for sequence alignment, evolutionary analysis, and
phylogenetic tree construction.

## PURPOSE
- Perform evolutionary analysis.
- Construct phylogenetic trees.
- Analyze DNA and protein sequences.
- Estimate evolutionary distances.

## APPLICATIONS
- Phylogenetic analysis.
- Sequence alignment.
- Evolutionary studies.
- Comparative genomics.

## TREE TYPES
- Neighbor-Joining (NJ)
- Maximum Likelihood (ML)
- Maximum Parsimony (MP)
- UPGMA

## OUTPUT FILES
- Newick (.nwk)
- MEGA Session (.meg)
- Tree files (.mtsx)
- Image files (.png, .jpg, .pdf)

## FILES TO UPLOAD
- FASTA (.fasta, .fa)
- MEGA (.meg)
- Nexus (.nex)
- Phylip (.phy)

## IMPORTANT POINTS
- Supports both DNA and protein sequence analysis.
- Provides multiple methods for phylogenetic tree construction.
- Includes statistical tools such as bootstrap analysis.
- Widely used in evolutionary biology and bioinformatics.
